IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa-employment`

-- Fair Work Act 2009, ss 12-15AA, 15P, 23, 45, 65-65A, 67-84, 87-96, 111, 114-123, 382-389, 530, 536, 536KL-536KMA, 544-548 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_fair-work-act-2009.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts are from the Western Australian scenarios (subjects/au/scenarios) where they exist; figures marked HYPOTHETICAL are
-- invented for the case and are not the real regulated amounts.

`Jake riding for the platform (k040)` MEANS PlatformWorker WITH
    `individual party performing work under a services contract` IS TRUE
    `performs all or a significant majority of the work` IS TRUE
    `work is through a digital labour platform and paid` IS TRUE
    `works under the contract as an employee` IS FALSE
    `low bargaining power` IS TRUE
    `paid at or below a comparable employee` IS FALSE
    `low authority over the work` IS TRUE
    `has a prescribed characteristic` IS FALSE

`a rider with only low bargaining power` MEANS PlatformWorker WITH
    `individual party performing work under a services contract` IS TRUE
    `performs all or a significant majority of the work` IS TRUE
    `work is through a digital labour platform and paid` IS TRUE
    `works under the contract as an employee` IS FALSE
    `low bargaining power` IS TRUE
    `paid at or below a comparable employee` IS FALSE
    `low authority over the work` IS FALSE
    `has a prescribed characteristic` IS FALSE

